-- title:
--   Theta certificate data, base range
-- statement:
--   Certificate records for the base range: segments of odd numbers covering $[3, 3594641)$, each with fixed-point lower and upper bounds for $Q\,\theta$ at its two ends ($Q=2^{64}$), starting from the bounds for $Q\log 2$.
--
--   The data are produced by a program and are checked, not trusted: the theorem `ThetaCert.base` states that the kernel checker accepts every record.
-- source:
--   P. Dusart, Estimates of some functions over primes without R.H., arXiv:1002.0442 (2010), Theorem 5.2 (k = 2, η = 0.2, x ≥ 3 594 641); here the range [3 594 641, 3 584 912 847] is closed by a kernel-checked sieve certificate.

import Definitions.Def_ThetaCertCore

